menu "Cranpose"

    config CRANPOSE_HOT_CODE_IN_IRAM
        bool "Run the framework's per-frame code from IRAM"
        default y
        help
            Links the framework functions that a frame runs most into IRAM,
            where the CPU fetches them without waiting for the flash or PSRAM
            cache. A frame of the demo then takes about half the time. The
            code takes 128 KB of internal RAM on the ESP32-S3, where IRAM and
            the heap share it, and 64 KB of the classic ESP32's IRAM, which
            its heap only lends to 32-bit allocations. Turn it off for an
            application that needs that memory more.

endmenu
